Pillbox is free software in the sense of "free of charge", not open source. This licence
says what you may and may not do with it.

1. What you may do

   You may download Pillbox from its official GitHub page
   (https://github.com/DAVe4954/Pillbox), install it, and use it free of charge on any
   number of computers, at home or at work.

   You may tell others about Pillbox and share the link to its official GitHub page.

2. What you may not do

   Unless the copyright holder has allowed it in writing, you may not:

   a. copy, publish, share, sell, rent or otherwise distribute Pillbox, its installer or its
      source code, in whole or in part, outside its official GitHub page;
   b. change, translate or adapt Pillbox or its source code, or make other software based on
      it;
   c. use any part of the source code in another project;
   d. charge anyone for Pillbox, or for access to it;
   e. remove or change this licence, the copyright notice or the other notices that come
      with Pillbox.

   Where the law of your country gives you a right that this section takes away (for example
   to study how a program works), that right stays yours.

3. The source code on GitHub

   The source code is public so that anyone can see what Pillbox does. Seeing it gives no
   permission beyond this licence. GitHub's own terms let GitHub users view and fork public
   repositories on GitHub; that does not allow anything in section 2.

4. Parts made by others

   Pillbox is built with open-source libraries made by others. Each is used under its own
   licence; they are listed, with their licence texts, in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt. This
   licence does not limit any right those licences give you for those parts.

5. No warranty

   Pillbox is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. See TERMS.md (the Terms of Use)
   for the full wording and the limits of liability.

6. Ending

   This licence ends by itself if you break it. You must then remove Pillbox from your
   computers. Sections 2 to 6 continue to apply after it ends.

7. Questions

   To ask for a permission this licence does not give, open an issue on the official GitHub
   page.
